/-!
# `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` is generated by a single perfect object

Let `X` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space over a scheme `S` and let
`T ⊆ |X|` be a closed subset such that `|X| ∖ T` is quasi-compact. Stacks 0AEC says that the
category `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` of objects of `D(𝒪_X)` with quasi-coherent cohomology sheaves
supported on `T` is generated by a single perfect object: there is a perfect object `P` of
`D(𝒪_X)` supported on `T` such that an object `E` of `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_X)` is zero if and only if
`Hom(P[n], E) = 0` for all `n ∈ ℤ`.

## The proof

This is the source's proof, by the induction principle of Stacks 08GP.

*Affine case.* An affine algebraic space is `h_{V₀}` for an affine scheme `V₀`; there the Koszul
complex on equations of the closed subset is a generator (Derived Categories of Schemes, Stacks
0A9A), carried to the small étale site through Stacks 071Q
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isSupportedPerfectGenerator_of_isAffineSpace`).

*Inductive step.* Let `(U ⊆ W, f : V ⟶ W)` be an elementary distinguished square with `V` affine,
and `P` a perfect generator of `D_{QCoh,T∩U}(𝒪_U)`. Stacks 09IV gives a perfect `Q` on `W`
supported on `T` with `P` a direct summand of `Q|_U`. On `V` there is a perfect `K` supported on
`f⁻¹(T ∩ (W ∖ U))` against which restriction to `U ×_W V` is bijective
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.restrictBijectiveAgainst_edsSnd`, the source's use of 09IR and 08DF on
`V`); its extension by zero `K' = f_!K` is perfect (Stacks 08HK, 08GG) and supported on `T`. The
generator is `Q ⊕ K'`. If `E` in `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_W)` receives no nonzero map from a shift of it,
then `Hom(K[n], E|_V) = Hom(K'[n], E) = 0`, so restriction from `V` to `U ×_W V` is bijective on
maps into `E|_V`. Hence every map `Q|_U ⟶ E|_U[m]` glues (Stacks 08HB) with a map on `V` to a map
`Q ⟶ E[m]`, which is zero; so `Hom(P[m], E|_U) = 0` and `E|_U = 0` by the choice of `P`. Then
`E|_{U ×_W V} = 0`, so `E|_V = 0` by bijectivity, and `E = 0`. The source phrases the middle step
as "`E = R(U → X)_* E|_U`"; the glueing statement is that identity read on morphisms out of `Q`,
and it avoids the derived direct image along `U ⟶ W`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isSupportedPerfectGenerator`: the generator, in the form of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsSupportedPerfectGenerator`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isPerfect_generator_of_supported`: **Stacks 0AEC**.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AEC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AEC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08GP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08GP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08HB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08HB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9A)
-/

